            <ArticleTitle>[A myocardial infarction in a patient with numerous coronary artery aneurysms].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>204-6; discussion 207</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of a 53-year-old smoking patient with myocardial infarction, in whom coronary angiography revealed many coronary arteries aneurysms, without substantial epicardial vessel narrowings. Patient was medically treated with a good outcome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
